{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b5d7c2c9-6904-4c7e-abb9-4813a5a3fd7e",
    "name": "Turkcell Open Gateway Documentation Teknofest",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "8365013"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Authorization (OIDC)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Authorization Code Flow",
          "item": [
            {
              "name": "1st Authorization request",
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "prerequest",
                  "script": {
                    "exec": [
                      ""
                    ],
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "packages": {},
                    "requests": {}
                  }
                },
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "exec": [
                      "if (pm.response.code === 302) {",
                      "    const locationHeader = pm.response.headers.get(\"location\")",
                      "    const url = new URL(locationHeader)",
                      "    const codeValue = url.searchParams.get(\"code\")",
                      "",
                      "    if (codeValue) {",
                      "        console.log(\"authorization_code\", codeValue);",
                      "        pm.environment.set(\"authorization_code\", codeValue)",
                      "    } else {",
                      "        throw new Error(\"Error occured! Check Location header for details.\");",
                      "    }",
                      "} else {",
                      "    throw new Error(\"Response Code is not 302!\");",
                      "}",
                      ""
                    ],
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "packages": {},
                    "requests": {}
                  }
                }
              ],
              "protocolProfileBehavior": {
                "followRedirects": false
              },
              "request": {
                "auth": {
                  "type": "noauth"
                },
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{api-gateway-url}}/oauth2/authorize?response_type=code&redirect_uri={{application-backend-callback-url}}&client_id={{application-client-id}}&state=realState&scope=openid dpv:RequestedServiceProvision%23quality-on-demand:sessions:create dpv:FraudPreventionAndDetection%23number-verification:verify",
                  "host": [
                    "{{api-gateway-url}}"
                  ],
                  "path": [
                    "oauth2",
                    "authorize"
                  ],
                  "query": [
                    {
                      "key": "response_type",
                      "value": "code",
                      "description": "Must be set to code."
                    },
                    {
                      "key": "redirect_uri",
                      "value": "{{application-backend-callback-url}}",
                      "description": "The callback URL of your backend server."
                    },
                    {
                      "key": "client_id",
                      "value": "{{application-client-id}}",
                      "description": "The unique identifier assigned to your application during registration."
                    },
                    {
                      "key": "state",
                      "value": "realState",
                      "description": "Anything that needs to be shared between your front and back ends will be included in the redirect to your redirect_uri"
                    },
                    {
                      "key": "scope",
                      "value": "openid dpv:RequestedServiceProvision%23quality-on-demand:sessions:create dpv:FraudPreventionAndDetection%23number-verification:verify",
                      "description": "Space-separated list of permissions. For Number Verification, use openid dpv:FraudPreventionAndDetection#number-verification:verify."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "description": "This is the 1st request of the Auth Code flow.\n\nBefore building the request, verify the correct API-specific scope required by the target service in the **Service APIs** documentation. For example, the Number Verification API requires the following scope:\n\n`dpv:FraudPreventionAndDetection#number-verification:verify`\n\n##### Request Parameters\n\nThe `openid` scope is mandatory for all OIDC authorization requests and must always be included in the `scope` parameter.\n\nIf additional API scopes are required, they must be added to the same `scope` parameter and separated by spaces.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```\nopenid dpv:FraudPreventionAndDetection#number-verification:verify\n\n ```\n\n##### **Testing the Authorization Request**\n\nSending it from Postman just won't work, since the client must follow redirections until reaching the `redirect_uri`. In order to test it, copy the URL resolved with your values and paste it in your browser running on the end-user's device.\n\nYou will need to publish an HTTP server to listen for the `redirect_uri` where the code will be redirected to."
              },
              "response": []
            },
            {
              "name": "2nd Get access token with client secret",
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "exec": [
                      "var jsonData = JSON.parse(pm.response.text());",
                      "pm.environment.set(\"access_token\", jsonData.access_token);"
                    ],
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "packages": {},
                    "requests": {}
                  }
                }
              ],
              "request": {
                "auth": {
                  "type": "basic",
                  "basic": [
                    {
                      "key": "password",
                      "value": "{{application-client-secret}}",
                      "type": "string"
                    },
                    {
                      "key": "username",
                      "value": "{{application-client-id}}",
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [],
                "body": {
                  "mode": "urlencoded",
                  "urlencoded": [
                    {
                      "key": "grant_type",
                      "value": "authorization_code",
                      "description": "Fixed value for this authentication method",
                      "type": "text"
                    },
                    {
                      "key": "code",
                      "value": "{{authorization_code}}",
                      "description": "The one obtained at the redirect_uri provided to /authorize",
                      "type": "text"
                    },
                    {
                      "key": "redirect_uri",
                      "value": "{{application-backend-callback-url}}",
                      "description": "You will take de authorization code at this endpoint from the code parameter in the query string",
                      "type": "text"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{api-gateway-url}}/oauth2/token",
                  "host": [
                    "{{api-gateway-url}}"
                  ],
                  "path": [
                    "oauth2",
                    "token"
                  ]
                },
                "description": "This is the 2nd request of the Auth Code flow.\n\nThis request is supposed to be performed from your backend, from where you publish your `redirect_uri` listening for the code requested in the 1st step.\n\nIn case the purpose used in the 1st step needed end-user consent, it will redirect such first request to the proper consent capture web page previous to the redirect to your redirect_uri."
              },
              "response": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "description": "This section describes the authorization flows that can be used to access CAMARA APIs:\n\n- Authorization code flow (Frontend flow) - Used to obtain a Three-Legged Access Token from the Authorization Server and initiated from the Consumption Device"
    },
    {
      "name": "Service APIs",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Number Verification",
          "item": [
            {
              "name": "v1.0.0",
              "item": [
                {
                  "name": "Number Verification verify",
                  "request": {
                    "method": "POST",
                    "header": [],
                    "body": {
                      "mode": "raw",
                      "raw": "{\n    \"phoneNumber\": \"+905390000020\"\n}",
                      "options": {
                        "raw": {
                          "language": "json"
                        }
                      }
                    },
                    "url": {
                      "raw": "{{api-gateway-url}}/number-verification/v1/verify",
                      "host": [
                        "{{api-gateway-url}}"
                      ],
                      "path": [
                        "number-verification",
                        "v1",
                        "verify"
                      ]
                    },
                    "description": "Use the frontend Auth Code flow in the Authorization folder to get an access_token, with the following purpose:\n\n`dpv:FraudPreventionAndDetection#number-verification:verify`"
                  },
                  "response": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Quality on Demand",
          "item": [
            {
              "name": "v1.1.0",
              "item": [
                {
                  "name": "QoD session",
                  "event": [
                    {
                      "listen": "test",
                      "script": {
                        "exec": [
                          "var jsonData = JSON.parse(pm.response.text());",
                          "pm.environment.set(\"qod_session_id\", jsonData.sessionId);"
                        ],
                        "type": "text/javascript",
                        "packages": {},
                        "requests": {}
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "request": {
                    "method": "POST",
                    "header": [
                      {
                        "key": "x-correlator",
                        "value": "test-correlation-id",
                        "type": "text"
                      }
                    ],
                    "body": {
                      "mode": "raw",
                      "raw": "{\n    \"duration\": 60,\n    \"applicationServer\": {\n        \"ipv4Address\": \"0.0.0.0/0\"\n    },\n    \"qosProfile\": \"teknofest2026\"\n}",
                      "options": {
                        "raw": {
                          "language": "json"
                        }
                      }
                    },
                    "url": {
                      "raw": "{{api-gateway-url}}/quality-on-demand/v1/sessions",
                      "host": [
                        "{{api-gateway-url}}"
                      ],
                      "path": [
                        "quality-on-demand",
                        "v1",
                        "sessions"
                      ]
                    },
                    "description": "Create QoS Session to manage latency/throughput priorities\n\nUse any of the flows in the Authorization folder to get an access_token, with the following purpose:\n\n`dpv:RequestedServiceProvision#quality-on-demand:sessions:create`"
                  },
                  "response": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "description": "This API requires the API consumer to identify a device as the subject of the API as follows:\n\n- When a three-legged access token is used however, this optional identifier MUST NOT be provided, as the subject will be uniquely identified from the access token."
        }
      ],
      "description": "Turkcell Open Gateway",
      "auth": {
        "type": "bearer",
        "bearer": [
          {
            "key": "token",
            "value": "{{access_token}}",
            "type": "string"
          }
        ]
      },
